f3ce34a0 (555 1793254820659 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f362") (src . "test: signal!'s identity guard gets its own rows; W5c releases on the retry\n\nTwo fixture changes.\n\ndaemon-idle and daemon-namespace send signals only to a registered process\nwhose start instant still matches (signal!), but no row showed the guard\nrefusing anything: removing the instant comparison changed no reading.\nEach fixture gains a control row: a perl sleep is registered, its\nrecorded start is altered, and signal! must answer already-gone with the\nprocess still alive; under its true start the signal is sent and the\nprocess goes. The sleep names the run's scratch directory, so the\nteardown reaches it, and it ends by itself after thirty seconds.\n\ndaemon-idle's W5c released the held old daemon after a fixed 1.5 s, so a\nmachine whose daemon start outlasts that sleep reached the lock after the\nrelease, with no retry to count. The release now waits for the shell's\ntrace to show the third spawn (the second request's first start and its\nretry), polled every 20 ms for at most thirty seconds.\n\n- test/daemon-idle.sc, test/daemon-namespace.sc: the rows.\n- test/row-baseline-check.sh: its header's counts.\n- test/rows-baseline.txt: the two fixtures' lines.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 502))))
