2a039d94 (573 1793256966478 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f374") (src . "supply keeps .gitignore by init's rule and refuses one that is not a file\n\nsupply adds /derived/ to the store's .gitignore. It decoded the file as\nUTF-8 to compare and wrote the decoded text back, so bytes that were not\nUTF-8 were replaced, and it asked a type that follows links, so a\n.gitignore that was a link was replaced and a directory failed after the\ntable's directory was made. The rule now lives once, in store.sc, for\ninit and supply alike: the file is merged as bytes (only the lines it\nlacks are appended, one carriage return at a line's end set aside to\ncompare), its name is looked at once, and a .gitignore that is not a\nregular file is refused. supply looks before it makes the table's\ndirectory or its lock, so a refusal writes nothing. Answers on success are\nunchanged.\n\n- store.sc: gitignore-merge, gitignore-kind and gitignore-refusal; init\n  uses them as before.\n- derived.sc: supply-derived refuses before its lock; ensure-ignored!\n  merges through gitignore-merge.\n- README: the supply sentence says so.\n- Tests: supply (non-UTF-8 kept, CRLF and an end-of-file CR, a link and\n  a directory refused with nothing made); unreadable-census;\n  rows-baseline.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 503))))
